1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,910
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,380
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,280
(Episode 37)

4
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,920
Oh, ma'am!

5
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,590
This was the very last one,

6
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:23,230
and it looks like it was waiting
just for you.

7
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:26,730
It looks so pretty on you. Really.

8
00:00:28,870 --> 00:00:29,870
It does?

9
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:33,370
If it didn't look good,
I'd have you take it right off.

10
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:35,340
This was made for you.

11
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:37,780
See? The color really
flatters your complexion.

12
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,440
You love it, don't you?

13
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:45,420
I do like it,
but the color is so vibrant...

14
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:48,850
With such a lovely face and figure,

15
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:52,220
if you don't wear this
pretty dress now, when will you?

16
00:00:52,220 --> 00:00:54,760
Many women can't wear this style...

17
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:57,900
even if they want to
because of their figure.

18
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:04,570
Today is the most beautiful day
of your life.

19
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:07,110
You must buy it, all right?

20
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:09,470
Pay in cash,
and I'll give you a discount.

21
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:12,040
It looks expensive.

22
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,910
With the discount, it's 113 dollars.

23
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:20,890
You don't dress up like this often,
do you?

24
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,890
Your husband's eyes might wander.

25
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,420
You know, he could cheat on you.

26
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:36,270
Here's 120 dollars.
Give me my change.

27
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:37,440
Sure.

28
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,200
And by the way, ma'am,

29
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:42,170
my husband cheated on me
a long time ago.

30
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,340
You must be new
to this neighborhood.

31
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:49,010
Just about everyone around here
already knows.

32
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:50,720
Oh, I'm so sorry, ma'am.

33
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:56,050
I own the place down the street,
Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.

34
00:01:57,660 --> 00:01:59,960
Since you gave me a discount,
I should return the favor.

35
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:01,290
Stop by sometime.

36
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:03,460
I will.

37
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,710
(Investment Agreement)

38
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:15,840
Do Yun's mother.

39
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:19,540
You pulled off a difficult task.

40
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:23,920
She worked really hard
on this, Mother.

41
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:27,150
Summit Two Partners
had such demanding conditions...

42
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:28,750
for the contract.

43
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,660
You said examining every clause...

44
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:32,920
closely was hard, right, honey?

45
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:39,300
It wasn't easy, Mother.
It took a bit longer than expected.

46
00:02:40,670 --> 00:02:44,270
Well, I didn't expect much myself.

47
00:02:46,470 --> 00:02:47,740
You did a great job.

48
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,310
- Excuse me?
- Well done.

49
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:56,610
You must have been deeply hurt...

50
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:58,180
that I had a background check
done on you,

51
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:00,750
and I heard from Do Yun's father...

52
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:03,960
just how upset you were.

53
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,560
Mother.

54
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:09,430
Now,

55
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:14,200
tell me what you want most
right now.

56
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:16,430
I will grant you anything.

57
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,940
Mother is asking.
Honey, you can speak freely.

58
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:29,750
What I want most right now, Mother,

59
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,520
is to have him...

60
00:03:35,790 --> 00:03:37,660
reinstated to his former position.

61
00:03:38,660 --> 00:03:42,030
That is the only thing
I ask for, Mother.

62
00:03:42,630 --> 00:03:43,630
Please.

63
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:51,270
I was thinking of making him reflect
for about a year.

64
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,770
Still, I cannot ignore your request.

65
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:59,510
However, you must do things
properly this time.

66
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:04,280
Yes, Mother,
I have reflected deeply.

67
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,520
I will not disappoint you.

68
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:30,880
Gosh, 113 dollars.

69
00:04:33,310 --> 00:04:34,750
I must have lost my mind.

70
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:38,520
How often will I even wear this?

71
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,590
Why did I agree to go see a play
in the first place?

72
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:50,760
I should return it.

73
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:53,230
Right,

74
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,970
I should call Dr. Ju to apologize.

75
00:05:01,910 --> 00:05:05,010
Where did I put my phone?

76
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,080
Seriously,
I definitely bought four cans...

77
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:13,180
for 12 dollars...

78
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,950
and stashed three,
so where did they go?

79
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:21,990
He's my enemy, not my brother.

80
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:26,060
How did my sister-in-law
put up with him all these years?

81
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:29,470
Darn it.

82
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:36,040
You scared me.

83
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,340
Who's there? Mom?

84
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,320
What are you looking for?

85
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:46,450
I cannot find my phone.

86
00:06:03,170 --> 00:06:05,970
How are you already
forgetting things like this?

87
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:07,770
Are you lecturing
your mother right now?

88
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:11,640
You had better remember
how much debt you owe.

89
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:14,750
I live under crushing pressure,
checking every penny...

90
00:06:15,350 --> 00:06:16,880
as the interest piles up day by day.

91
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,350
Is that so?

92
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:23,120
Yet you still find the time
to flirt with a young woman.

93
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,630
- I am so proud of you, my son.
- I told you, it is not like that.

94
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:29,560
She is just a girl I know.

95
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,630
Mi Mi, I need to close up,
but the cash register...

96
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,900
is way off. Could you...

97
00:06:38,700 --> 00:06:40,470
What are you wearing?

98
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:42,940
Can you not tell?

99
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,910
I bought a new one.

100
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:48,910
- It caught my eye.
- You paid money...

101
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:51,620
to buy that outfit?
It is not Da Mi's?

102
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,320
What about it?

103
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,890
Can I not wear a dress like this?

104
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:57,260
No,

105
00:06:58,190 --> 00:06:59,960
it is just weird hearing you say...

106
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,260
you bought an outfit like that
out of nowhere, that is all.

107
00:07:03,290 --> 00:07:05,700
Is that not for women?

108
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,300
Hey, I am a woman too.

109
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,540
I bought women's clothes
because I am a woman.

110
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,200
No, that is not what I meant.

111
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:17,040
Come on, you're a mom,
not some young woman.

112
00:07:17,180 --> 00:07:20,380
Besides, outfits like that are meant
for young women.

113
00:07:21,050 --> 00:07:22,910
Do not get mad.

114
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:28,190
Still, the color is a bit too bright
for someone your age.

115
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:31,960
Why don't I try it on
instead? It's okay, right?

116
00:07:32,490 --> 00:07:33,490
No.

117
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:35,860
- Mi Mi.
- Mom.

118
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:39,000
I said no. This is mine.

119
00:07:41,430 --> 00:07:42,800
I am wearing it, you brats.

120
00:07:44,470 --> 00:07:45,470
Good grief...

121
00:07:49,710 --> 00:07:51,080
Aunt Ri Ja, what is her problem?

122
00:07:52,310 --> 00:07:53,310
She is weird.

123
00:08:00,650 --> 00:08:01,650
Excuse me.

124
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,620
Yes, ma'am?

125
00:08:03,890 --> 00:08:05,090
Are you heading out to work already?

126
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:07,330
I need to speak with you
for a moment.

127
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,360
Of course.

128
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:13,830
How has Mother been doing lately?

129
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:16,130
Pardon?

130
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,240
Once I leave for work
in the morning,

131
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,640
I do not get to see her all day.

132
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:22,740
The one who spends
the most time with her...

133
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,040
in this house is you.

134
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:26,910
Do you understand what I mean?

135
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:31,780
Usually, when it is sunny,
she sits out in the garden with me,

136
00:08:32,050 --> 00:08:36,050
or we take a walk in the park.
Her stamina seems fairly good.

137
00:08:36,990 --> 00:08:38,920
I see. That is a relief.

138
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:42,460
Take this.

139
00:08:43,430 --> 00:08:44,630
What is this?

140
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:48,400
Her mind slips in and out.

141
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:52,400
Madam Ma, who worked here before,
had a very hard time with that.

142
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,610
Excuse me.

143
00:08:55,170 --> 00:08:58,540
Please continue
to take good care of Mother.

144
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:00,980
And...

145
00:09:02,450 --> 00:09:04,820
whom she talks to on the phone,

146
00:09:05,450 --> 00:09:06,920
what they talk about,

147
00:09:07,450 --> 00:09:10,920
I need you to report all of that
to me separately in detail.

148
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,030
Report on
what Madam Chairwoman does?

149
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:17,700
The more I know about your work,

150
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,360
the better I can reward you.

151
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,070
More than just what you work for,

152
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,570
I want to take care of you
generously.

153
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:25,940
And I will.

154
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:30,170
Understood.

155
00:09:31,110 --> 00:09:33,640
- Thank you, ma'am.
- Just...

156
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,150
keep this one thing in mind.

157
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,250
Mother can get very upset...

158
00:09:39,380 --> 00:09:43,290
if she feels her children
are prying into her business.

159
00:09:43,990 --> 00:09:48,130
So do not mention this to her,
and keep it discreet.

160
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,760
Clear?

161
00:09:50,230 --> 00:09:51,260
Yes, ma'am.

162
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,740
Mother, I am heading to work.

163
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:01,910
You do not need to come in.

164
00:10:02,410 --> 00:10:03,980
Watch out for cars.

165
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,740
Yes, Mother.

166
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,680
Let us go, honey.

167
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,050
I should tell Mother I am leaving.

168
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,190
I already did, so it is fine.

169
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:19,120
How does it feel to go back to work?

170
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:23,030
Thanks to you,
my suspension ended early,

171
00:10:23,090 --> 00:10:24,530
so it feels surreal.

172
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:28,430
Still, waking up in the morning
and having somewhere to go...

173
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,100
makes me deeply grateful.

174
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:33,100
Thank you. It is all thanks to you.

175
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:34,870
Come on, let us get going.

176
00:10:36,410 --> 00:10:38,510
- Have a good day.
- Yes.

177
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:48,890
(Cashier's Check: 10,000 Dollars)

178
00:10:49,390 --> 00:10:51,490
Wait, 10,000 dollars,
not 1,000 dollars?

179
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,360
Ones, tens, hundreds...

180
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:58,230
- I'm heading out now, ma'am.
- All right.

181
00:10:58,530 --> 00:10:59,530
Where are Mom and Dad?

182
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,330
They just left.

183
00:11:02,370 --> 00:11:03,370
There you are.

184
00:11:06,900 --> 00:11:08,270
Heading to work now?

185
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:10,110
- Yes, Grandma.
- Right.

186
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,840
Is there anything you'd like to eat?
I'll pick it up on my way home.

187
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:17,420
Could you buy me
some scorched-rice candy?

188
00:11:18,050 --> 00:11:19,620
Grandma, just candy?

189
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:21,320
- Yes.
- He's capable of so much more.

190
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:23,390
Ask him for something pricier
and more delicious.

191
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:28,390
Candy is enough for me.
Have a good day, both of you.

192
00:11:28,490 --> 00:11:30,130
Yes, Grandma. I'll make sure
to bring the candy.

193
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,260
All right, sounds good.

194
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:39,840
Please look after Grandma today.

195
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:42,510
And if anything comes up,
please call me.

196
00:11:56,450 --> 00:11:58,120
Excuse me, ma'am.

197
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,720
Yes?

198
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:02,260
What is it?

199
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:05,760
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

200
00:12:16,510 --> 00:12:17,510
Head Designer Cha.

201
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:19,680
Are you asleep?

202
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:22,450
Head Designer Cha?

203
00:12:24,280 --> 00:12:26,880
Man, he wouldn't even notice
if someone carried him off.

204
00:12:28,090 --> 00:12:29,790
This is so frustrating.

205
00:12:33,190 --> 00:12:34,530
I would notice
if someone carried me off.

206
00:12:35,530 --> 00:12:38,130
You startled me.
Weren't you sleeping?

207
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,360
When you haven't turned in
your assignment,

208
00:12:40,430 --> 00:12:42,200
how could your superior
possibly sleep?

209
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:45,770
Head Designer Cha,

210
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:48,870
I tried desperately,
looking through references,

211
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,880
analyzing, and agonizing over it.

212
00:12:51,510 --> 00:12:53,610
"My skills as an assistant
aren't enough."

213
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:54,910
Is that what you're trying to say?

214
00:12:56,350 --> 00:13:00,780
But you couldn't find
an answer either, Head Designer Cha.

215
00:13:03,690 --> 00:13:04,690
I'm sorry.

216
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:11,200
No, you're not completely wrong.
Still, Da Mi,

217
00:13:12,130 --> 00:13:14,370
when your mentor
can't find the answer...

218
00:13:14,470 --> 00:13:15,670
and is struggling,

219
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,040
if the assistant is lost as well,

220
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:21,340
would the mentor really have
any use for an assistant like that?

221
00:13:23,370 --> 00:13:24,380
No.

222
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:27,480
I will keep searching for an answer
in my own way,

223
00:13:27,550 --> 00:13:31,080
but that's my job.
And in your role as an assistant,

224
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:33,250
you must deliver
your own results to me.

225
00:13:33,550 --> 00:13:34,550
That's your job.

226
00:13:35,950 --> 00:13:37,050
Yes, Head Designer Cha.

227
00:13:38,690 --> 00:13:39,690
Wait, hold on a second.

228
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:40,960
Yes?

229
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:45,200
Why have you been
wearing that jacket this whole time?

230
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:48,670
I thought wearing it might help me
spot whatever the problem is,

231
00:13:48,730 --> 00:13:52,370
so I've had it on since yesterday.
The shoulders aren't uncomfortable,

232
00:13:52,670 --> 00:13:55,740
and the waistline is tapered nicely
to make the legs look longer,

233
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:58,610
so I truly have no idea
why it didn't sell.

234
00:14:01,010 --> 00:14:02,050
Hold on. Stay right there.

235
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,180
Why? What is the matter?

236
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,190
Let me see.

237
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,860
If the sleeves were just a bit
longer, it would look better.

238
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,260
Why do the sleeves look so short?

239
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:20,230
Could it be because...

240
00:14:20,230 --> 00:14:22,870
my arms and legs are
on the longer side?

241
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:30,870
What?

242
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,240
(Access Pass)

243
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,440
What is it? What is wrong?

244
00:14:34,510 --> 00:14:36,410
Just a moment, sir.

245
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,290
Mom, where are you going?

246
00:14:48,790 --> 00:14:51,230
I told you I have a gathering
with the merchants association.

247
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,240
Why take it off? It looks nice.

248
00:14:58,670 --> 00:15:01,110
What good is looking nice?

249
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:04,340
Did they give up halfway
making these pockets?

250
00:15:04,910 --> 00:15:06,710
Are they skimping on fabric here?

251
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:09,650
See? Look at this.

252
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,450
It does not even fit.

253
00:15:13,050 --> 00:15:14,550
- My gosh.
- Kang Da Mi?

254
00:15:17,050 --> 00:15:18,290
I found it.

255
00:15:18,860 --> 00:15:20,660
I think I found the problem.

256
00:15:21,260 --> 00:15:22,260
Found what?

257
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:24,900
The main problem...

258
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,600
with Hwanggeum Apparel's...

259
00:15:27,670 --> 00:15:28,970
spring and summer items...

260
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,500
from last year and this year...

261
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,200
is the pockets.

262
00:15:34,670 --> 00:15:35,670
The pockets?

263
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,410
What's wrong with the pockets?

264
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:39,740
They are only pockets in appearance.

265
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,980
Look. This one is way too shallow.

266
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:46,350
And this one is too narrow.

267
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:50,450
This blouse is the same way.
It has pockets,

268
00:15:50,790 --> 00:15:52,260
but the problem is...

269
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:53,890
that they cannot even serve
their most basic function.

270
00:16:04,640 --> 00:16:06,740
Right? Am I not right?

271
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:10,140
Well...

272
00:16:10,810 --> 00:16:15,110
Ms. Kang, I'll take
your idea into consideration.

273
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,150
Wait, why are you following me? Why?

274
00:16:22,890 --> 00:16:23,890
Are you not going downstairs...

275
00:16:23,950 --> 00:16:25,160
for the meeting
in the design studio?

276
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,760
No, I am going to the restroom.

277
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:29,330
- Go ahead, sir.
- All right.

278
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:38,270
Are pockets really not the issue?

279
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:41,970
I am sure pockets
are the problem, though.

280
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:48,380
Unbelievable.
She actually figured it out.

281
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:51,820
Interesting.

282
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:56,520
So, what do you think?

283
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:01,630
What did you tell the housekeeper?

284
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,190
Fortunately,

285
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:07,130
she seems to understand
what matters more than money.

286
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:10,500
Your daughter-in-law
probably thinks...

287
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:12,540
she can easily control
someone like a housekeeper...

288
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,600
with money.

289
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:17,440
I pretended to give in, but...

290
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:19,610
Do Yun's mother...

291
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:22,350
will keep a closer watch on me.

292
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,720
Especially after
she dropped the bombshell...

293
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:29,190
that her name was Jeon Jin Sook
before joining my household.

294
00:17:30,690 --> 00:17:32,190
You must be careful.

295
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:34,560
Even if it is inconvenient
for the time being.

296
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:37,090
I will stop by from time to time.

297
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:41,170
And find out about Jeon Jin Sook.

298
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:45,270
Look into when
and where Do Yun's mother...

299
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:47,040
lived under that name.

300
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:52,410
Do not let your footsteps be heard,
or your shadow be seen.

301
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,180
Yes, Madam Chairwoman.

302
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:56,610
Right.

303
00:17:58,920 --> 00:17:59,920
Very well.

304
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:01,950
Oh my.

305
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:04,760
Did your appointment go well,
Mrs. Hwang Geum Soon?

306
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,460
When would you like to schedule
your next visit?

307
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:10,290
I will call ahead
on the day I plan to come.

308
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:14,930
- Dr. Ju, I will see you around.
- Yes.

309
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,130
No need to see me out.

310
00:18:16,770 --> 00:18:19,170
- Take care on your way back.
- All right.

311
00:18:21,170 --> 00:18:22,470
See you next time, ma'am.

312
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,580
Have a great day.

313
00:18:29,680 --> 00:18:30,680
Dr. Ju.

314
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:34,020
That's Hwanggeum Capital's...

315
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,790
chairwoman Hwang Geum Soon, right?

316
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:37,550
This person here.

317
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,260
(Hwang Geum Soon, Businessperson)

318
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,860
How do you know
who she is, Ji Young?

319
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:45,430
My daughter is an assistant manager
at Hwanggeum Apparel.

320
00:18:45,900 --> 00:18:49,730
I know everything there is to know
about the Hwanggeum family.

321
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:53,640
My goodness,
she looks so graceful in person...

322
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:57,510
for someone her age.
Her aura is simply...

323
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:02,250
- Are you two close?
- I am just her primary physician.

324
00:19:02,910 --> 00:19:05,150
(Doctor's Office)

325
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:07,480
Oh my.

326
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:11,220
That means she will keep coming
to our clinic.

327
00:19:12,290 --> 00:19:15,030
I should strike up a conversation
and get close to her.

328
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,190
Making a good impression
cannot hurt.

329
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:18,400
All for our Ye Ri.

330
00:19:21,530 --> 00:19:22,970
Have you lost your mind?

331
00:19:23,270 --> 00:19:26,240
No, I have not.
I have never been clearer-headed.

332
00:19:27,070 --> 00:19:29,940
Why must you talk to your own wife
like that?

333
00:19:30,140 --> 00:19:32,040
I already opposed you
being so desperate...

334
00:19:32,110 --> 00:19:35,710
to set Ye Ri up
with someone from a rich family.

335
00:19:35,780 --> 00:19:38,980
At the clinic, you'll befriend...

336
00:19:39,050 --> 00:19:42,390
- Ye Ri's company chairwoman?
- It's a golden opportunity.

337
00:19:44,290 --> 00:19:47,590
Did you forget what
the kids' mother said?

338
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:49,030
Their mother? Who?

339
00:19:49,530 --> 00:19:52,130
- Jo Mi Mi?
- Yes, my ex-wife.

340
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,830
The owner of Mi Mi's Chicken Soup.

341
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,930
The landlord of the building
where you work.

342
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:00,800
Why would that be a problem?

343
00:20:02,070 --> 00:20:03,340
You said you wanted
to make money, right?

344
00:20:03,710 --> 00:20:06,080
Then please, just quietly
do your job at the clinic, okay?

345
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:10,710
Do not make a fuss
and put Ye Ri in an awkward spot.

346
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:13,920
You are giving me anxiety.

347
00:20:16,350 --> 00:20:17,720
If I don't get caught, who cares?

348
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:27,430
I'm sorry.

349
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:30,030
(Small Conference Room)

350
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:33,940
He said he was going
to the restroom.

351
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,470
Why is he not back yet?

352
00:20:35,810 --> 00:20:37,740
Why is he not answering
his phone either?

353
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:41,810
What if he collapsed
somewhere again?

354
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:49,090
Even if I bought new clothes,

355
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:52,860
these sneakers are the only
decent pair of shoes I have.

356
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,790
These will not do at all.

357
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:06,370
Da Mi used to wear these.

358
00:21:16,310 --> 00:21:18,450
- Mom.
- Sweetheart.

359
00:21:18,650 --> 00:21:21,120
Could I borrow your heels...

360
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:23,690
- from my shoe rack for a day?
- My heels?

361
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,960
Of course you can.
We wear the same shoe size anyway.

362
00:21:27,290 --> 00:21:28,730
Did you really call
just to ask that, Mom?

363
00:21:29,330 --> 00:21:32,400
Thank you.
I will just wear them for a day.

364
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,930
By the way, did you eat yet?

365
00:21:36,430 --> 00:21:38,640
You must still be at work.

366
00:21:39,370 --> 00:21:41,000
All right, I will let you go.

367
00:21:58,090 --> 00:21:59,990
Do your feet get bigger as you age?

368
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:02,460
They feel a little tight.

369
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:06,900
Wait.

370
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:09,100
Mom is wearing heels?

371
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:13,440
You and your mother seem very close,
Manager Kang.

372
00:22:14,970 --> 00:22:16,040
CEO Jeon.

373
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,840
My mistake.

374
00:22:18,410 --> 00:22:21,110
I was just so used to calling you
Manager Kang for so long.

375
00:22:21,810 --> 00:22:22,810
It is all right.

376
00:22:23,310 --> 00:22:25,380
How is it working
as Jaden Cha's assistant?

377
00:22:25,950 --> 00:22:27,420
I imagine it is not easy.

378
00:22:27,820 --> 00:22:30,490
Though, of course,
that is just my guess.

379
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,920
I believe that no job
is easy at first, CEO Jeon.

380
00:22:34,290 --> 00:22:37,230
I consider it a great opportunity
and I am doing my best.

381
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,100
Keep up the good work, then.

382
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:45,340
By the way, Manager Kang...

383
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,440
Kang Da Mi.

384
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:50,110
- Yes?
- In my opinion,

385
00:22:50,540 --> 00:22:52,580
luxury manager
at the department store...

386
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:55,310
suits you much better, Kang Da Mi.

387
00:22:57,710 --> 00:22:58,720
Pardon?

388
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:02,490
Those textbook answers
ingrained in you.

389
00:23:02,750 --> 00:23:04,290
That polite smile and poise.

390
00:23:04,890 --> 00:23:07,090
But in the fashion industry...

391
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,430
I'm a little concerned.

392
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:14,060
Bullets might not be flying,

393
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,900
but every single day
is a war zone here.

394
00:23:24,110 --> 00:23:25,240
Mom...

395
00:23:25,710 --> 00:23:27,410
What is your daughter
supposed to do?

396
00:23:28,750 --> 00:23:30,410
That was kind of scary.

397
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:37,790
(Cha Do Yun, Team Leader)

398
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:41,290
I will take off first,
Assistant Manager Kang.

399
00:23:41,360 --> 00:23:42,660
Let us head down together,
Team Leader Cha.

400
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:47,260
There you are.

401
00:23:47,930 --> 00:23:50,400
Have you happened to see
my assistant?

402
00:23:50,730 --> 00:23:51,970
She hasn't come here.

403
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:53,600
Really?

404
00:23:54,370 --> 00:23:56,770
- Where could she have gone?
- Have you called her?

405
00:23:57,440 --> 00:24:00,180
Yes, I did try calling,
but her phone is turned off.

406
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:01,710
I sent a message too, but no reply.

407
00:24:02,580 --> 00:24:05,020
Could it be that she ran off...

408
00:24:05,480 --> 00:24:06,550
because you gave her
such a hard time?

409
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:10,150
She didn't run off.

410
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:12,020
I made sure her bag was still there
before coming.

411
00:24:16,490 --> 00:24:20,060
Were you here, sir?
I was looking everywhere for you.

412
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:22,530
Are you serious right now?

413
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:25,100
That's what I should be asking you!

414
00:24:25,170 --> 00:24:28,210
Why was your phone turned off?
Get back to the office right now.

415
00:24:28,240 --> 00:24:29,370
We have a mountain of work to do.

416
00:24:31,070 --> 00:24:32,680
Did you call me?

417
00:24:33,510 --> 00:24:34,780
When did it turn off?

418
00:24:35,180 --> 00:24:38,250
Well, the battery was probably due
to die, so it shut off on its own.

419
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:48,860
Working overtime all night
will be exhausting.

420
00:24:50,130 --> 00:24:51,230
For Kang Da Mi?

421
00:24:52,630 --> 00:24:53,730
For both of them.

422
00:25:06,540 --> 00:25:08,710
I need to make money right away.

423
00:25:09,950 --> 00:25:12,950
Should I just bite the bullet
and take whatever job I can get?

424
00:25:16,490 --> 00:25:17,550
Kim Pro,

425
00:25:18,820 --> 00:25:21,420
I will catch you, darn it.

426
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:28,000
Channel that anger...

427
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,000
into a determination
to get back on your feet.

428
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,070
Show it through your actions,
Dae Chi.

429
00:25:35,570 --> 00:25:37,710
Why call me Dae Chi
when she barely knows me?

430
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:46,480
Hey.

431
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:50,090
What are you thinking about
that has you grinning like that?

432
00:25:52,890 --> 00:25:53,990
Who said I was grinning?

433
00:25:54,890 --> 00:25:55,960
Hey, Gang Nam.

434
00:25:56,630 --> 00:25:58,130
Did Da Mi really move out for good?

435
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:00,400
I thought she would be back,
but she has not returned.

436
00:26:00,530 --> 00:26:03,200
What has gotten into you?
Since when do you care about her?

437
00:26:04,370 --> 00:26:05,640
Am I not her older brother?

438
00:26:10,910 --> 00:26:11,910
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

439
00:26:13,010 --> 00:26:14,040
Thank you for the meal.

440
00:26:15,010 --> 00:26:17,580
Sure. Come again.

441
00:26:25,660 --> 00:26:27,660
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

442
00:26:31,660 --> 00:26:33,560
What on earth am I doing right now?

443
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:36,600
Darned habit of greeting everyone.

444
00:27:21,950 --> 00:27:22,950
Ma'am.

445
00:27:25,280 --> 00:27:26,480
Am I a bit late?

446
00:27:26,980 --> 00:27:29,020
No, I just came outside myself.

447
00:27:35,730 --> 00:27:36,730
Does it look weird?

448
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:40,230
I decided to splurge and bought it.

449
00:27:40,900 --> 00:27:42,530
Not at all, it looks great on you.

450
00:27:43,300 --> 00:27:44,370
Shall we go?

451
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Sure.

452
00:28:07,020 --> 00:28:08,690
(Mission: Mompossible)

453
00:28:09,190 --> 00:28:12,400
Why isn't she answering her phone?
It is not like she is on a date...

454
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:14,760
- with some slick-looking guy.
- Does Mi Mi have a boyfriend?

455
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:17,570
Why don't you try them on first
to see if they fit?

456
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:18,900
Hello?

457
00:28:18,970 --> 00:28:21,040
She was so quiet,
I thought something happened.

458
00:28:21,140 --> 00:28:23,310
Wait, why am I worrying
about that rich brat?

459
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:26,710
I want her to leave on her own feet,
but is there a way to make her quit?

460
00:28:27,810 --> 00:28:29,810
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
